WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:09.059 --> 00:00:13.730
wait a minute Neanderthals are extinct

00:00:14.150 --> 00:00:21.390
before you laugh check yourself
Neanderthal DNA is 99.7% identical to

00:00:21.390 --> 00:00:26.730
our own and researchers claim that some
humans might be carrying as much as 2%

00:00:26.730 --> 00:00:32.279
of the Neanderthal genome making things
even weirder is that scientists recently

00:00:32.279 --> 00:00:37.680
recovered a nearly complete DNA sequence
from a 50 thousand year old Neanderthal

00:00:37.680 --> 00:00:44.370
skeleton so in theory Neanderthals could
make a comeback but how would they adapt

00:00:44.370 --> 00:00:51.839
and how long would they survive this is
what if and here's what would happen if

00:00:51.839 --> 00:00:57.780
Neanderthals hadn't gone extinct despite
their physical differences like being

00:00:57.780 --> 00:01:01.350
shorter and having longer skulls we
might have more in common with

00:01:01.350 --> 00:01:05.760
Neanderthals than we'd like to admit
first of all their brains were bigger

00:01:05.760 --> 00:01:09.840
which doesn't make them smarter than us
but they could communicate with one

00:01:09.840 --> 00:01:13.920
another they settled in family
communities and took care of the sick

00:01:13.920 --> 00:01:17.490
and the elderly
they also crafted sophisticated tools

00:01:17.490 --> 00:01:21.930
which would have been used for anything
from hunting to possibly shipbuilding

00:01:21.930 --> 00:01:26.960
and they even cook their vegetables and
ate them which is more than you can say

00:01:26.960 --> 00:01:32.820
so if Neanderthals are simply the beta
version of what humans became could they

00:01:32.820 --> 00:01:39.420
still live among us Neanderthals in fact
did live among us for about 5,000 years

00:01:39.420 --> 00:01:45.450
Homo sapiens and Neanderthals coexisted
in Europe and likely interbred this

00:01:45.450 --> 00:01:49.799
would explain why most Eurasians
probably have at least 1% of the

00:01:49.799 --> 00:01:54.390
Neanderthal DNA in their genome while
any one of African descent doesn't have

00:01:54.390 --> 00:01:58.579
any Neanderthal DNA since their
ancestors didn't migrate through Eurasia

00:01:58.579 --> 00:02:03.869
but with the homo sapien population
significantly outnumbering in the and

00:02:03.869 --> 00:02:07.920
earth all population it's likely that
modern humans simply absorbed the

00:02:07.920 --> 00:02:13.050
Neanderthal species another theory is
that we out competed them for resources

00:02:13.050 --> 00:02:18.510
during the last ice age resulting in
their extinction but whichever theory is

00:02:18.510 --> 00:02:25.040
right what if the concluding fact was
what if Neanderthals were not extinct

00:02:25.040 --> 00:02:30.319
if Neanderthals somehow evolved as a
separate but very similar species to

00:02:30.319 --> 00:02:34.580
humans how would they fare
despite their communication and

00:02:34.580 --> 00:02:38.750
craftsmanship abilities the laws of
natural selection prove that Homo

00:02:38.750 --> 00:02:43.129
sapiens are superior which means the
survival options for Neanderthals

00:02:43.129 --> 00:02:47.480
wouldn't be that great barring the
likelihood of early modern humans

00:02:47.480 --> 00:02:51.620
breeding them out of existence
Neanderthals probably would have become

00:02:51.620 --> 00:02:57.700
something like second-class citizens
would we enslave them keep them in zoos

00:02:57.700 --> 00:03:03.019
or force them to fight it's hard to say
with the limits of their intelligence

00:03:03.019 --> 00:03:07.609
prevent them from fully integrating into
modern society or would they learn and

00:03:07.609 --> 00:03:13.120
evolve just like Homo sapiens
maybe they'd want nothing to do with us

00:03:13.120 --> 00:03:17.299
realizing how our differences outweigh
our similarities could we expect

00:03:17.299 --> 00:03:21.049
Neanderthals to establish their own
communities and continue to exist

00:03:21.049 --> 00:03:25.549
independently of the developing world
it's hard to predict exactly how a

00:03:25.549 --> 00:03:30.709
species that went extinct about 40,000
years ago would behave today but then

00:03:30.709 --> 00:03:35.810
again maybe we just have to look around
us Neanderthals may be extinct but we

00:03:35.810 --> 00:03:41.329
did evolve alongside them and some of us
inherited more than others so think

00:03:41.329 --> 00:03:45.019
twice before you call someone a
Neanderthal it can be quite offensive

00:03:45.019 --> 00:03:52.660
and for more enlightening topics stay
tuned for more what if

